<title>UK: BOE gives money mkt 625 mln stg help at set rates.</title>
<headline>BOE gives money mkt 625 mln stg help at set rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with 625 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    750 MLN    750 MLN    900 MLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    =	    =	    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    =	    625 MLN*   =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>The Bank will offer a round of unspecified late assistance at some point after 1430 GMT. Click on  RTCC or type RTCC and Enter to see details.</p>
</text>
